ic  return we saw that Jets from stars and  stripes's Squadron flying in the sky  above Deku chapter 367 confirms that the  objects that had approached Deku back in  chapter 357 were in fact members of the  Stars and Stripes Squadron members who  disobeyed direct orders to leave Japan  and instead they decided to stay here  and help fight the villains in any way  that they could that is a pretty big  deal since these are members of the  American armed forces who decided to go  Rogue in order to help fight in another  country something like that would be  massive news if it ever happened here in  our own world but in a world with  superheroes and super villains it's just  like a passing side note Deku had used  black whip to grab onto one of the Jets  and he was pulled back to UA much faster  than he would have been able to arrive  otherwise I for one am glad that this  happened because at this crucial stage  of the story the Final Act of the story  having Deku not playing any sort of  important role for six months in real  time just doesn't seem right to me like  we had three major battles going on at  the same time with the fate of all of  Japan and the world at stake I guess  four battles if you want to count okuto  Island although I don't think we should  count dokudo Island and yet Deku the  main character was stuck flying out  there somewhere off the coast of Japan  and he was unable to contribute to any  of the battles but Deku is finally back  now and after getting a pep talk from  the Squadron Pilots about the need for  Deku to honor the memory of stars and  stripes by taking down the greatest  villain to ever live we are taken back  to the present where Deku is already  engaging in battle against Apex Legend  the shigaraki Deku manages to land a  blow on shigaraki and the villain can  already tell the Deku seems stronger  than he was before Deku has definitely  gotten stronger since he last faced  shigaraki injaku and he has unlocked new  quirks we can assu