ine and put him out of  commission for good as we all know by  now all for one loves to engage in  psychological warfare he loves to psych  his opponents out which leads to the  opponents losing their cool and making  mistakes and is exactly what he's hoping  is going to happen to Deku we saw  something similar happening to Endeavor  a few chapters ago when he lost his cool  and made a hasty move but thankfully  Meteo is still conscious and after last  week's peachy super move he jumps in  with yet another overpowered super move  in fact this is one of the most  overpowered super moves in the history  of anime manga talk no Jutsu Meteo tells  Deku that it's all right he knows  exactly how Deku feels and he also feels  terrible about the fact that he wasn't  able to do more to protect everyone who  got her but meteor also tells daku that  the situation is not as bad as it looks  despite being severely injured all the  heroes on the battlefield are still  alive they are all still breathing and  although bakugou is technically dead Ed  shot is currently working to revive him  from the inside Meteo says that he's  sure Ed shot will succeed so even though  they've suffered some losses none of  these losses are actually permanent  everyone can and still make it out a lot  the important thing that Deku has to  remember now is that all for one wants  him to lose his cool and make a stupid  mistake so Deku has to overcome his rage  and keep his emotions in check there is  still hope so Deku can't give up he has  to keep his wits about him and he has to  fight smart all for one slash shigaraki  says that this is naive idealism and  it's nothing but a silly fantasy but  Meteo screams that if anyone can turn  fantasy into reality it's the heroes and  they are heroes these words remind Deku  of the lessons that all might and the  previous users of one for all had taught  him he is also reminded of the members  of stars and stripes Squadron who  disobeyed orders because they beli