le to the death situation  such as this one controlling your  emotions perfectly is almost impossible  and I mean from a storytelling  perspective let's be real we all want to  see shigaraki at full power with the  full use of all his quirks going up  against Deku at full power and with all  of his quirks unlocked so I do think  that some something will happen that  will break monoma's Erasure and allow  shigaraki to reach his full potential at  some point in the future if shigaraki  can figure out a way to get to izawa he  might be able to kill two birds with one  stone he will stop the Erasure at least  eventually and at the same time he will  enrage Deku leading to him losing  control and acting recklessly at that  point even deku's final Quirk whatever  it turns out to be may not be enough to  stop shigaraki in his Apex Legend form  and with all his quirks fully functional  including super regeneration that is  when I believe that all of deku's quirks  will suddenly merge into one single  ultimate Quirk Deku will reach Quirk  Singularity and his body will then also  evolve in a somewhat similar way to  shigaraki it won't be exactly the same  as shigaraki because he had all those  ujiko modifications and Deku simply  didn't but at the same time Deku has  less quirks than all of all for one's  stolen works so we'll see how it goes we  will then see the greatest single clash  in the history of mha as full power  final form shigaraki goes up against  full power Quirk Singularity Deku and  that is going to be absolutely epic that  at least is my theory for how this whole  thing will ultimately end but let me  know what your theories are down below  my biggest worry is that Deku is going  to try too hard to save tanko shimura  who is hiding somewhere within shigaraki  something that this latest chapter even  hinted at and I believe that this could  lead to some sort of anticlimactic talk  no Jutsu ending or it could lead to Deku  making the mistake of going easy on  s